     "It comes to 8.75 %, below the real 11 %. The mistake is that this average treats leisure (which has not risen and is only 10 % of spending) the same as housing (which has risen 20 % and is 30 %). Households feel the 11 %, because what has risen most is precisely what weighs most in their spending."
