       "GDP = 3,000, rfne = 140, rfen = 200 (€ million): $$\\mathrm{GNP}=3{,}000+140-200=2{,}940$$ GNP is lower than GDP because foreign factors earn more here than ours earn abroad. It is the typical case of a country with a lot of foreign investment. Ireland is the best-known example: many foreign multinationals have their headquarters there, and the profits they take away make its GNP clearly lower than its GDP."
