       "**Step 1. Classify** $$\\mathrm{LF}=\\mathrm{EP}+\\mathrm{UP}=1{,}050+150=1{,}200\\qquad \\mathrm{IP}=\\mathrm{TP}-\\mathrm{LF}=2{,}000-1{,}200=800$$ **Step 2. Calculate the rates** $$\\text{Unemployment rate}=\\frac{150}{1{,}200}\\times 100=12.5\\%$$ $$\\text{Activity rate}=\\frac{1{,}200}{2{,}000}\\times 100=60\\%$$ $$\\text{Dependency rate}=\\frac{1{,}050}{2{,}000}\\times 100=52.5\\%$$ The typical mistake would have given $\\frac{150}{2{,}000}\\times 100=7.5\\%$ unemployment."
